Reverts helium/core/search/fix-search-engine-icons.patch (GPL-3.0, The Helium Authors): built-in search provider
assets are on only for Chrome-branded builds again, as in Chromium. The build doesn't fetch Helium's non-free
search engine assets (third_party/search_engines_data/resources_internal), and the setting isn't a GN argument,
so a gn arg can't turn it off.

--- a/build/config/chrome_build.gni
+++ b/build/config/chrome_build.gni
@@ -111,4 +111,4 @@
 
 # Whether to enable built-in branding assets (logos & marketing snippets) for
 # search providers in choice UIs.
-enable_builtin_search_provider_assets = true
+enable_builtin_search_provider_assets = is_internal_chrome_branded
